tion/Hardware-Abstractions-14","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions#network-on-chip-noc","content":"Cores and shared resources connect through an on-chip network, such as a 2D mesh. The NoC handles data exchange between cores and provides access to global shared memory."},"19":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions-15","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions#global-memory","content":"A shared memory stores neural network weights, feature maps, activations, and intermediate results accessible by all cores."},"20":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions-16","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions#global-memory","content":"**Synchronous Inter-Core Communication**: Transfers between cores are blocking. A core waits until the transfer completes before continuing execution."},"21":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions-17","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions#core-level","content":"Each core has its own compute units, local memory, and register files."},"22":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions-18","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions#memory","content":"Global and local memories share a unified address space. Local memory uses a segmented layout with dedicated regions for input and output data."},"23":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions-19","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions#unit-level","content":"Each core contains three types of compute units:"},"24":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions-20","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions#cim-compute-unit","content":"The CIM unit performs matrix-vector multiplication (MVM) in SRAM arrays. It contains **K** macro groups, each with **T** macros (both are architecture parameters)."},"25":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions-21","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions#cim-compute-unit","content":"Each macro group operates independently for data parallelism. Macros within a group share input data but store different weights, organized along the output channel dimension."},"26":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions-22","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions#vector-compute-unit","content":"The vector unit handles element-wise operations after MVM: quantization, activation functions (ReLU, Sigmoid, Tanh), partial sum accumulation, residual addition, and pooling."},"27":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions-23","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Hardware-Abstractions#scalar-compute-unit","content":"The scalar unit handles control flow and address generation: computing load/store addresses, conditional and unconditional branches, loop counters, and barrier-based synchronization for multi-core coordination."},"28":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/ISA","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/ISA","type":"page","content":"Instruction Set Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Abstraction","ISA"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Abstraction/ISA"},"29":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/ISA-0","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/ISA","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/ISA","content":"Programming interface for SRAM-based CIM accelerators"},"30":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/ISA-1","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/ISA","type":"heading","tags":[],"