al_code.json` regardless of the internal pass ordering."},"303":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend-43","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend#mlir-pass-pipeline","content":"For background on the MLIR framework and pass infrastructure, see the official documentation at mlir.llvm.org/docs."},"304":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend-44","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend#mlir-pass-pipeline","content":"The five pass groups run in sequence:"},"305":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend-45","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend#init-passes-toc","content":"Inlining, canonicalization, symbol cleanup, function-level CSE, alias folding, affine lowering, and memory address allocation"},"306":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend-46","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend#lower-passes-toc","content":"CIM dialect lowering, canonical optimizations, and common subexpression exposure"},"307":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend-47","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend#unroll-passes-toc","content":"Loop unrolling and cleanup/canonicalization"},"308":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend-48","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend#rr2ricf-passes-toc","content":"Register-form rewriting, SCF-to-CF conversion, branch lowering, and offset/constant optimizations"},"309":{"id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend-49","page_id":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Compiler/DSL-and-MLIR-Backend#codegen-pass-toc","content":"Emit final ISA JSON (`final_code.json`)"},