ading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#transfer-runtime-stages","content":"Transfer Runtime Stages"},"1549":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-5","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#issue-toc","content":"Issue [!toc]"},"1550":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-6","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#read-toc","content":"Read [!toc]"},"1551":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-7","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#write-toc","content":"Write [!toc]"},"1552":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-8","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#sendrecv-handshake-toc","content":"SEND/RECV Handshake [!toc]"},"1553":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-9","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#sender-ready-toc","content":"Sender Ready [!toc]"},"1554":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-10","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#receiver-ready-toc","content":"Receiver Ready [!toc]"},"1555":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-11","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#data-transfer-toc","content":"Data Transfer [!toc]"},"1556":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-12","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#complete-toc","content":"Complete [!toc]"},"1557":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-13","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#synchronization-through-transfer-path","content":"Synchronization Through Transfer Path"},"1558":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-14","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","content":"Transfer-related instructions map to memory domains, runtime data paths, and NoC costs based on the address-space configuration."},"1559":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-15","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#address-space","content":"All transfer decode decisions are based on the `AddressSpace` configuration. For each source and destination address, the simulator resolves three things:"},"1560":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-16","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#address-space","content":"If the address-space mapping is incorrect, the simulator will resolve addresses to the wrong memory region or fail at startup. Verify mappings in Input Files before debugging transfer behavior."},"1561":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-17","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#transfer-types","content":"The simulator decodes each transfer instruction into one of five types based on the source and destination addresses."},"1562":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-18","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#data-path-selection","content":"For local transfers, the `DataPathManager` checks configured memory-pair mappings:"},"1563":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-19","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#data-path-selection","content":"If `(src_mem_id, dst_mem_id)` matches a configured dedicated pair, the transfer uses a `local_dedicated_data_path`"},"1564":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-20","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#data-path-selection","content":"Otherwise the transfer falls back to `intra_core_bus`"},"1565":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-21","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#data-path-selection","content":"Global load/store and inter-core send/receive always use `inter_core_bus`. Dedicated data paths are defined in `transfer_unit_config.local_dedicated_data_path_list`."},"1566":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-22","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#transfer-runtime-stages","content":"Each transfer instruction passes through three stages inside the `TransferUnit`."},"1567":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-23","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#transfer-runtime-stages","content":"Local transfers use `LocalTransferDataPath` with batch splitting. Each batch transfers up to `max(src_read_width, dst_write_width)` bytes, using the wider port width as batch size. The total number of batches is `ceil(size_byte / batch_max_data_size_byte)`."},"1568":{"id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer-24","page_id":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Simulator/Memory-Network-Transfer#issue-toc","content":"Create per-batch payloads from the full transfer request"},"1569":{"id":"/docs/Si