a register and an 11-bit signed immediate value (−1024 to 1023)."},"2006":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation-19","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation#sc_ri","content":"Append **I** for immediate variants (e.g., `ADD` → `ADDI`)"},"2007":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation-20","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation#sc_ld","content":"Loads a value from local memory into a general register using base+offset addressing."},"2008":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation-21","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation#sc_st","content":"Stores a register value to local memory using base+offset addressing."},"2009":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation-22","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation#g_li","content":"Loads a 21-bit unsigned immediate (0 to 2,097,151) directly into a general register."},"2010":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation-23","page_id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Design/Instruction-Set/Scalar-Operation#s_li","content":"Loads a 21-bit immediate into a special register. Used to configure CIM array and Vector unit parameters before compute operations."},"2011":{"id":"/docs/Abstraction/Instruction-Desi